/**
@mainpage Nocturne Engine C++ API

# Start here

If you are learning Nocturne, open @ref api_beginner_guide before browsing the
alphabetical class list.

This API reference is intentionally written to explain **what a type does, when you
should use it, when you should not use it, ownership/lifetime, threading assumptions
and common call flow**.

# Primary subsystem groups

- @ref runtime
- @ref world_ecs
- @ref resources
- @ref rendering
- @ref editor

# Purpose

This site is the generated C++ reference for the current Nocturne Engine header surface.

Use the canonical Nocturne documentation for the larger architecture, subsystem
boundaries and design rationale:

- Human documentation: `/docs/`
- Machine knowledge manifest: `/knowledge/manifest.json`
- Canonical AI aggregate: `/llms-full.txt`
- Doxygen XML: `/api-xml/index.xml`

# Source precedence

For current behavior, use:

1. canonical Architecture / Systems / Development documentation;
2. current C++ source for exact implementation behavior;
3. completion/implementation reports as delivered-work evidence;
4. historical Phase documents for chronology and earlier design context.

Doxygen is an explanatory symbol layer. It does not override canonical architecture
documentation.

# Extraction policy

The beginner-facing reference includes public/protected API surface from current
Engine, NocturneEditor and NocturneHost headers.

Private class members are deliberately hidden from the primary reference so internal
implementation details do not overwhelm the API you are expected to use.

The following are also deliberately excluded:

- `ThirdParty/`;
- test directories;
- `Engine/Render/DX12/d3dx12.h` because it is vendored DirectX helper code;
- legacy `EditorShell.h` and `EditorControls.h`, because `EditorShellV3` is the
  current canonical editor shell.

@note Design choice (not directly from the book): Doxygen is the generated C++
reference layer and Web 7.1 makes the default view beginner-oriented. The supplied
engine books ground subsystem concepts and architecture, not this documentation-tool
choice.
*/

